virtual valkyrie) says:
>
>Hi gang.  I've got a problem with my newly installed 3.1.3.  Even
>if my screen shows, say, 11 spell points, I will be told that I am too
>weak to cast "that spell" --  no matter what the spell in question is.

Spell-casting is hungry work.  If your stomach is not properly filled,
you are too weak from hunger to cast the spell.  Notice that being too
weak to cast a spell is a much more common state than being too weak
to carry your stuff around.

>Once I've gotten massive amounts of spell points, I can begin to cast,
>but each spell seems to be eating up 6 or 7 times the number of points
>it should.  It doesn't show more thatn the normal deduction on the
>display; I just can't cast anything.

It's using just the right number of spell points (i.e. you Are using
just as many points as the bottom line says you are).  Take another
look at your hunger status.

